BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Rebel Craft Collective": "https://www.meetup.com/the-rebel-craft-collective/events/314772439/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_rebel_craft
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Rebel Craft Collective
UID:event_314772439@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260521T024848Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T193000
SUMMARY:Happy Hour Crafts
DESCRIPTION:The Rebel Craft Collective\nWine + tasty snacks + your latest project and a friendly group of likeminded crafters... what better way to unwind? Come join us!\n\nThis is a relaxed\, drop-in-friendly event. Come when you can\, leave when you must. Newcomers and occasional-comers are always welcome!\n\n**What do we mean by “crafts”?**\nWhatever “craft” means to you! And whatever is portable enough to bring to a wine bar. Knitting\, crochet\, and other fiber arts are most common\, but we have also warmly welcomed people who sketch\, color\, embroider\, bead\, and more. If your craft isn’t portable\, we will happily ooh and aah over photos of your work-in-progress\, or chat about your plans for your next project.\n\n**Health & Safety**\nMasks are very welcome\, and nobody will pressure you to eat or drink. If the weather is nice\, we will try to sit outside. If you aren’t eating/drinking during the event\, please consider ordering some of La Dolce Vita’s delicious food to-go\, in order to help support our gracious\, long-time venue.\n\n**Parking**\nParking in downtown Petaluma is free\, but street parking has a strictly enforced 2 hour limit until 6pm. To park for longer\, try the nearest garage:\n\n* The Second Street Garage entrance is located on C Street between First and Second Streets. It's all day parking on every level and a short walk to La Dolce Vita.\n\n**Ages**\nIt's a wine bar\, so this event is for adult crafters (though you're certainly not required to drink wine!). We’re okay with babes-in-arms if you are\, but this is not the right setting for wee crafters who are moving about on their own.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-rebel-craft-collective/events/314772439/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260513T184124Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T184124Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/2/b/3/600_527801651.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petaluma Museum": "https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/from-past-to-future-stewarding-our-wetlands-together/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petaluma_museum
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T193000
DTSTAMP:20260520T194912
CREATED:20260513T194133Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T194505Z
UID:6427-1779991200-1779996600@www.petalumamuseum.com
SUMMARY:From Past to Future: Stewarding Our Wetlands Together
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging panel discussion with conservation leaders and community partners working across the Petaluma River watershed.\nDate:  Thursday May 28 6:00 – 7:30 pm\nVenue: Petaluma Historical Library & Museum\n20 4th Street (Corner of 4th & B St.)\nPetaluma\, CA 94952\nFree!  Reservations Appreciated\nHow have our relationships with Petaluma’s wetlands changed over time—and what does stewardship look like in a changing climate? \nJoin us for an engaging panel discussion connected to Time & Tide: An Artful Exploration of Petaluma’s Wetlands\, bringing together conservation leaders and community partners working across the Petaluma River watershed. \nTogether\, we’ll explore how this landscape has been shaped by both human activity and natural processes\, and how today’s efforts—grounded in restoration science\, Indigenous knowledge\, and community action—are helping to build a more resilient future. \nPanelists will share insights on: \n\nThe historical transformation of the watershed\nCurrent restoration and conservation efforts\nThe role of collaboration and community stewardship\nHow wetlands support climate resilience—reducing flood risk\, supporting biodiversity\, and helping our region adapt to rising seas\n\nThis conversation invites us to reflect on what it means to learn from the past\, act in the present\, and steward the wetlands we all depend on for the future. \nFree! RSVPS appreciated.
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/from-past-to-future-stewarding-our-wetlands-together/
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library & Museum\, 20 4th St\, Petaluma\, CA\, United States
CATEGORIES:Current Exhibit,Event,Exhibit Presentations
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/From-Past-to-Future.webp
END:VEVENT
