BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Floathouse": "https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/events/sup-yoga-on-the-petaluma-river-june-12-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:floathouse
SUMMARY:SUP Yoga on the Petaluma River 
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T193000
UID:863107f9015583de87f6d45cfacd8c40@thefloathousepetaluma.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63
 02d39abd02437a9e9f0276/1770414836353-TGPGBLBRPM49SRKDJJ1E/SUP+Yoga+2026+sq
 uarespace+calendar+image+%28no+dates%2C+just+April-October%29+%281500+x+10
 00+px%29.png
DESCRIPTION:SUNSET SUP Yoga on the Petaluma River\, “Petaluma’s Longes
 t Park” Step away from the rush and into the quiet of the Petaluma River
  for a peaceful SUP Yoga experience with The Floathouse Petaluma . And flo
 at into the sunset with us. Time to say goodbye to the week. Though we lau
 nch from the heart of downtown\, the central turning basin offers a surpri
 singly serene setting—calm water\, open sky\, and a sense of ease that f
 eels far removed from daily life. This all-levels\, 90-minute session is d
 esigned for everyone: experienced yogis\, seasoned paddle boarders\, and c
 omplete beginners alike. We begin with a short\, gentle paddle from the do
 cks to get comfortable on your board (knees are always welcome). Once we r
 each our practice spot\, we anchor together so tidal movement won’t inte
 rrupt your flow. From there\, you’re invited to move\, breathe\, rest\, 
 or simply be—guided by an experienced instructor and supported by the sh
 ared rhythm of water and community. All equipment is provided\, including 
 extra-stable paddleboards measuring 34 inches wide and 11 feet long—much
  larger than a yoga mat and designed to help you feel grounded and secure 
 on the water. Come as you are. Choose your own level of effort. Flow with 
 the river and the people around you. It’s YOUR river. Come out and play.
  $50/person\, includes all gear\, instruction\, and quality time on the wa
 ter. Book here. #block-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 { --stroke-style: none\;--stro
 ke-thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: initial\; } #bloc
 k-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 .sqs-html-content { --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 
 6% 6% 6%\; --tweak-text-block-padding: initial\; } #block-a001b972e87bc115
 5cc0 { mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend )\; border-radius: var
 (--tweak-text-block-radius)\; } #block-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 { --tweak-text
 -block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px\; } #block-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 { } @media 
 screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 { } } @media s
 creen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-a001b972e87bc1155cc0 .sqs-html-conte
 nt { } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { }
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma\, 50 Water Street\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/events/sup-yoga-on-the-petaluma-
 river-june-12-2026
X-SOURCE:The Floathouse Petaluma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"The Block Petaluma": "https://www.facebook.com/rambletone?mibextid=wwXIfr&mibextid=wwXIfr"}
X-SOURCE-ID:the_block_petaluma
SUMMARY:Rambletone Blues Revue
DTSTART:20260612T180000
DTEND:20260612T210000
UID:a8bc22c48b45898f@theblockpetaluma.com
DESCRIPTION:The “Rambletone” blues revue is a hoppin’\, groovin’\,
  funky\, bluesy band based in the San Francisco Bay Area. The members of R
 ambletone are Tony Lemieux on vocals\, guitar and harmonica\, Ian Luke on 
 drums\, Bob Fruhlinger on bass\, Stu Dahlquist on guitars\, Willy Gross on
  saxophone and John Snee on keyboards. Rambletone has a number of influenc
 es based in the blues\, rockabilly\, Americana\, a dash of raggae and funk
 y jams to boot\, such as: Muddy Waters\, Allman Bros\, SRV\, Stray Cats\, 
 Howlin Wolf\, Clapton\, Marley\, the Dead ect. You can find Rambletone’s
  music online on all your favorite streaming sites!\; Including their albu
 m “Remixed &amp\; Reimagined”. You can also find them tearing up stage
 s all around the Bay Area!
URL:https://www.facebook.com/rambletone?mibextid=wwXIfr&mibextid=wwXIfr
X-SOURCE:The Block Petaluma
END:VEVENT
